# 101CRUISE Development Rules

## Project Vision

101CRUISE is a premium cruise planning application with an Apple-inspired design.

The application should always feel:

- Clean
- Spacious
- Professional
- Calm
- Consistent

Never introduce clutter.

---

## Technology

Frontend:
- HTML
- CSS
- JavaScript

Hosting:
- Netlify

Planner Data:
- Supabase

CRM:
- Base44

---

## Brand Colours

Primary green: `#8DD9BF` (`--brand-green`)
Dark green for text/icons: `#245C4E` (`--brand-green-ink`)

Reuse established brand colours and existing design tokens in `css/planner.css` `:root` (hover, soft mint `#EFFAF6`, border). Do not invent new greens. Do not introduce new colours or redesign the established visual identity without Steve’s explicit approval. Do not restyle established accents (newsletter Other Info `#d9f2e8`, newsletter price `#1f7a66`) unless explicitly asked.

Customer checklist/progress rings use `#8DD9BF`.
The Hang-tight loading overlay uses the red nine-square logo (`#f80020`), not green.

---

## Design Standards

Cards must have:

- generous spacing
- rounded corners
- consistent padding

Typography should be restrained.

Avoid oversized headings.

Avoid bold buttons unless specifically requested.

---

## Customer Page Width

All customer-facing pages and major content sections must use the shared centred outer container:

- `--planner-content-width` (1180px)
- `--planner-content-gutter` (48px)
- Reuse `.planner-shell`, `.dashboard-content-wrap`, or the shared page classes already used by Dashboard, Preparation, Packing, Budget and Documents

Do not change the global shared page width rule. Only full-bleed hero sections may span edge-to-edge.

Inside that shared shell, dense information or form pages may use a narrower centred reading column so labels and values remain readable. The Booking page reading column uses `max-width: 760px`. Do not replace the outer shell with a page-specific maximum width.

---

## Coding Standards

Reuse existing components.

Do not introduce duplicate CSS.

Always explain which files were changed.

---

## Development Workflow

Before making changes:

1. Read the relevant files.
2. Understand the existing implementation and the root cause.
3. Make a focused, complete correction in the original module responsible for the behaviour.
4. Preserve existing behaviour unless instructed otherwise.

Never introduce patches, band-aids, temporary workarounds, duplicate implementations or hidden complexity. If the original implementation is wrong, fix it at the source. The nine Global User Rules continue to apply.

Never redesign completed modules unless requested.

GitHub repository `swmummery-commits/101cruise-planner` is the authoritative repository, with `main` as the baseline. Before editing application code, verify whether an approved development branch contains newer work. Check the current GitHub branch and local changes before editing. Do not treat historical uploads, a stale checkout, or README sprint notes as authoritative over GitHub.
